          "score": 21.0,
          "snippet": "# 3.3 Crystal Growth Optimization\n\nSince we succeeded in growing small RhSeCl crystals via SSVG technique in the 'flipped' furnace, we then explored whether higher temperatures and a different temperature gradient could further enhance growth. To achieve this, we carried out SSVG in short ampules (6cm), with the end containing the precursors placed in the centre of a one-zone tubular furnace. This provided a small thermal gradient without inducing undesired CVT transport. We tested three precursor systems:  $\\mathrm{RhCl}_3$ -,  $\\mathrm{SeCl}_4$ -based\n\n![](images/5698ab5bd551b51314605af3569ed54863d9bbb6219c39caa3232c99d249e037.jpg)  \n(a)\n\n![](images/2b462bd1d57672f673b47456467fec8d3340831bc9a4a9da1d724cab9bc4e7f6.jpg)  \n(b)  \n(c)\n\n![](images/18ae525348dedb38677100270098a479019548198430b0"
        },
