          "line_start": 144,
          "line_end": 152,
          "score": 15.0,
          "snippet": "# 3.5 Comparison of the Crystal Growth Methods\n\nComparing all crystal-growth approaches reveals how both the reaction chemistry and the thermal environment govern the formation of high-quality RhSeCl crystals. Conventional CVT methods, as previously reported in the literature, reliably produces\n\nRhSeCl crystals, however, their size remains limited. CVT growth for RhSeCl occurs primarily through vapour transport between the hot and cold ends of the ampule, leading to agglomerates of small crystallites, while additional evaporation-condensation processes at the source can occasionally yield larger, isolated crystals. In contrast, the SSVG technique in a 'flipped' box furnace enables growth directly within a minimal temperature gradient, and when applied using  $\\mathrm{RhCl}_3$ -based precur"
